	)
	(text "Values ending in ? are placeholders - edit to what is on the breadboard.\n\nDetector: datasheet Fig. 3 half-wave peak detector. D1 replaced by Q2, a diode-connected\n2N3906 (emitter = anode, base + collector = cathode), so its drop tracks Q1's base-emitter drop.\nR5 + R6 replace Fig. 3's R3 (input to ground) and double as the peak-LED divider.\nAttack ~ R1 x C1 (C1 charges through R1); release ~ R2 x C1; 20 dB fall ~ 2.3 x R2 x C1.\nBase current returns through R5 + R6, so a high-impedance (switched-off) source lifts the reading.\n\nBar: full scale RHI = 1.25 V x (1 + R8/R7) + ~80 uA x R8 (REF OUT tied to RHI).\n0 VU lamp (pin 13) lights at 0.708 x RHI. Target: 3.474 Vpp sine (+4 dBu) = 0 VU.\nEach LED gets ~10 x (REF OUT load current); its shunt resistor bypasses about Vf / R of that.\nLED order: pin 1 = -20 VU ... pin 10 = +3 VU.\n\nPeak LED: U2 (TL071H) trips when PK_DIV > RHI, i.e. AUDIO_IN peak > RHI x (R5 + R6) / R6.\nC4 holds it on; it discharges through R9 into Q3's base (~0.5 s with 150k / 3.3u)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 271.78 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "80fc4438-3a48-4c28-a429-a128eb2ac28d")
	)
	(text "-3 VU  green"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 244.475 122.555 0)
